## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cryptomatteencode.html
- Summary (EN): Packs object-ID and coverage data into the Cryptomatte format, storing them in 32-bit RGBA layers. The page is inconsistent on outputs: its purpose text says it outputs one Mono coverage layer and one ID layer, while its output section names a single RGBA layer called crypto.
- Résumé (FR) : Encode des identifiants d'objets et leurs couvertures au format Cryptomatte, dans une couche RGBA 32 bits.

- Inputs meaning: ["id_a: hash value of the first object", "cov_a: coverage of the first object", "id_b: hash value of the second object", "cov_b: coverage of the second object"]

- Caveats: ["The page documents no parameters.", "The ID layer stores a hash of the object name; recovering names needs re-hashing or the EXR metadata.", "A Cryptomatte normally spans several RGBA layers read together; this node packs only one.", "Page is inconsistent on outputs (Mono coverage plus ID versus a single RGBA crypto layer)."]

